# The handle must resolve on the host this repository lives on, which is
# github.com. That was the whole difficulty on the tenant this repository moved
# off: its accounts were EMU-provisioned through Google SAML and shared no
# namespace with github.com, so a handle valid in one place existed in neither
# the other. GitHub silently ignores an owner it cannot resolve — an
# unresolvable owner does not fail the file, it just leaves every path unowned,
# which is indistinguishable from having no CODEOWNERS at all. `ops github
# setup` resolves every owner named here against the API for exactly that
# reason.
